JOT/JWT/Json(JavaScript notation object) Web Token:=> A JSON token that is used on web for authentication.

-> As we maintain Session to login once and use the same session throughout the application resources.
like - SSO(Single Sign On)-> GMAIL, GMeet, GDrive, etc...

But maintaining the same session for authentication may lead to threat of CSRF(Cross site req forgery).

=> Here comes JWT not XMLToken as they are bulky itself even after compression.
""""It is provided by server/ app/ web resources at the first call to server which
must/might be the login one except some open resources..""""

JWT Token => header( algo like HS(hMac)/RS(RSA), type: JWT ) + Body(sub,name,issue_Time,expiry_time) + signature
RSA and ES are Asymmetric key-cryptography(Use public key + private key concept)
HS -> Symmetric key same key

For, Creating signature we use cryptography either symmetric or Asymmetric algo...


Note: We do sent JWT over internet with request so everyone can see that.
=> It not ensure secrecy as it is visible and can be decoded using online tools
=> but provide accountability as ""no one can use it without signature/stamp""....

We can also secure token(JWT) using https instead of http => so we can achieve both secrecy and accountability...
